cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use linlog in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: linlog
abstract: >-
  A linear logic suite: a Rust library and a command line program that
  decide, check, prove step by step and export sequents of classical and
  intuitionistic linear logic and their fragments, keep proofs in a form
  an independent checker validates, show them as derivation trees or
  proof nets, and decide ordinary propositional logic through its
  embeddings into linear logic. Its code, tests and documentation were
  written with substantial AI assistance, by Anthropic's Claude models in
  Claude Code, in steps the author planned, directed and accepted, and
  the author is responsible for them. Its results do not rest on the
  model that wrote it: every proof it returns is validated by an
  independent proof checker, classical proofs can be exported as
  certificates that the Rocq proof assistant checks, the tests are
  measured by mutation testing and fuzzing, and its verdicts on
  published problem libraries are compared with their known status and
  with those of eight other provers.
authors:
  - given-names: Fabian Lukas
    family-names: Grubmüller
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-18"
license: EUPL-1.2
repository-code: "https://github.com/linlog-prover/linlog"
url: "https://linlog-prover.github.io/linlog/"
keywords:
  - linear logic
  - intuitionistic linear logic
  - proof search
  - sequent calculus
  - proof nets
  - theorem prover
